In a lab notebook entry, an auditor notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Determine the correct result here. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(30);
Node b = new Node(20);
Node c = new Node(25);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

In a reading group, an auditor notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Apply the concept to this instance. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {2, 3, 5, 9, 11, 16, 19, 21, 26};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 5) return mid; if (a[mid] < 5) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return -1; Which answer is correct for this case?

Use the facts presented to decide. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {1, 3, 4, 3, 0, -4};
int acc = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > acc) acc = a[i];
return acc;

In a reference guide, an auditor notes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Decide which option is correct. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ooedbo";
int acc = 0, target = 'i';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

The case below gives the figures. The following. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {3, 6, 9, 12, 13, 15, 19, 20, 23};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 38) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 38) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

